A||||17||FieroJoe||www.suspension.com - Who's bought from them?||||10||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||12-25-2001||10:47 PM||||Hey all, I've been comparing prices for total poly kits, and it comes to be that <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com" TARGET=_blank>www.suspension.com</A>  has the best deals.  They do not offer a total kit, like the Fiero Store (149.95), but they individual prices for the front, and rears are cheaper.<P>The front control arms set is $51, the rear control arm set is $26, engine cradle mounts are $48, dogbone (press in) bushings are $17.<P>Those are pretty good prices, which add up to $142 (shipping included, free)  They are prothane brand too!  I was thinking of getting all those listed things, which would be much less than FS and I get almost twice as more, seeing as I will need the cradle mounts and engine strut mount.  I will not need the swaybar hardware, since I have already converted mine to prothane, so there is almost no need to buy the total kit from FS.<P>First question:  I can only assume that the front and rear control arm sets are to do both sides, am I right in this assumption?  Or, will I have to order two of each?<P>Also, for those of you who have ordered from them, would you again?  Do they ship as fast as they say, do they have good customer service, and send you the right part the first time?<P>Thanks!<p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 12-25-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||Cooter||12-25-2001||10:59 PM||||I bought all my bushings from them a while back. The front end set comes with enough bushings for both sides, same for the rear set. I messed up when I ordered and had to send back one set and the replacement set from them got here before I sent the other ones back. Would I order from them again- you had better believe it!||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||12-25-2001||11:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B>I bought all my bushings from them a while back. The front end set comes with enough bushings for both sides, same for the rear set. I messed up when I ordered and had to send back one set and the replacement set from them got here before I sent the other ones back. Would I order from them again- you had better believe it!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Thats good to hear!  I am glad that I ran upon them, their prices are very nice.  Did you get all your bushings in red?  They say they stock all of them in black, but can get red...<P>Anybody else bought from them or found other places that might be cheaper?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-25-2001||11:43 PM||||Only place to buy them if you ask me... someone here had a cheaper place but had to go thru a bunch of crap as I recall to get them.<P>keep in mind.... only the original style dogbone will accept the polly. That's the one with a ridge around the outside of the loops.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||12-25-2001||11:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>keep in mind.... only the original style dogbone will accept the polly. That's the one with a ridge around the outside of the loops.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, I have pressed in the poly bushings to a stock dogbone for a 84 I restored for a guy.  I dont have any dogbone right now (engine didnt come with one) but I will try to find a 85-86 one that will accept the bushings.<P>Sounds like my descision has been made!<P>Now, should I go with poly dust boots or just get new rubber ones (the ones on there right now arent in the best of shape..)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spiff||12-26-2001||01:24 AM||||That's where I bought all my poly bushings from. IIRC The owner is a fiero enthusiast. Really nice man. I would buy from him again.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spiffsig2_4.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Nashco||12-26-2001||02:39 AM||||Yup, I support them as well.  I bought some red poly dogbone bushings and some front ball joints from them.  They had the best prices, very fast shipping, and when I called with questions they were very knowledgeable (rare with Fiero questions <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).  I'd buy from them again without a second thought.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||mshill||12-26-2001||12:50 PM||||Order complete sets for my two cars from them, going to order a third set this year for my sons restoration project.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Howard_Sacks||12-26-2001||01:38 PM||||I bought from suspension.com and had no problems.  The customer service was actually really good.  You might want to order cradle bushings too if you're putting all that other stuff in(I went for aluminium, but poly is probably fine too).  Also, you can get colors besides red if you ask.  I got my control arm bushings and some other stuff in black from them.<P><BR>Howard||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jimmy||12-26-2001||07:42 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com" TARGET=_blank>www.suspension.com</A>  rocks!  I bought front, rear, and cradle from them.<P>Jimmy<BR>87 GT T-TOP V8<BR>87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jncomutt||12-26-2001||08:05 PM||||Can you order online from them??  I found the poly I want, but the credit card order form doesn't seem to want to work for me.  Do I have to call or mail this in or something???||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fierobruiser||12-27-2001||12:29 AM||||Have you looked at any of 8SHARKS stuff?   <A HREF="http://www.8shark.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.8shark.com/</A> <P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)<P>[This message has been edited by Fierobruiser (edited 12-27-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Fierobruiser (edited 12-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||FieroJoe||12-27-2001||12:35 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierobruiser:<BR><B>Have you looked at any of 8SHARKS stuff?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I just did, and I am not impressed.  The prices are way up there, and by the picture of the bushings on the main page they don't look to be quality.  Are the bushings supposed to have the offset hole in them for the control arms?  Also, they don't even look to have been turned very well, because the bushing surface seems rough with grooves and lines on it. <P>I'm still going with poly from suspension.com!<p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 12-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||SCCA FIERO||12-27-2001||01:21 AM||||I ordered a set for the rear of my 88 from them. The guy I talked to was punching keys on his computer (I could hear it) and was talking to himself at the same time. When I told him what year and car I was ordering for, he said to himself, "That year didn't have control arms." I was surprised he knew that.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Fierobruiser||12-27-2001||01:22 AM||||The offset bushings, I believe, are to allow for greater than normal camber and caster adjustment particularly for lowered cars and or competition type suspension adjustment. They appear to be cleanly machined to me.<P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)||||reg||1
